Allow multiple row advances per tick when virtualTempoN > virtualTempoD.

The break after nextRow() was limiting row advances to at most one per engine
tick. When virtualTempoN > virtualTempoD (playback ratio > 1), the while loop
needs to be able to call nextRow() more than once per tick to achieve the
intended speed-up. Commenting out the break lets the accumulator continue
consuming ticks within the same loop iteration, enabling correct speed-up
behavior for ratios > 1.

diff --git a/src/engine/playback.cpp b/src/engine/playback.cpp
--- a/src/engine/playback.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/playback.cpp
@@ -2182,7 +2182,7 @@ bool DivEngine::nextTick(bool noAccum, bool inhibitLowLat) {
             }
             // ...and now process the next row!
             nextRow();
-            break;
+            //break;
           }
         }
         // under no circumstances shall the accumulator become this large
